{"name":"Rapture","hex":"#114444","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Rapture","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["In some forms of fundamentalist Protestant eschatology, a prophesied sudden removal of Christian believers from the Earth before the Tribulation or simultaneous with the second coming of Jesus Christ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Rapture"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rapture","blocks":[{"text":"The Rapture is an eschatological (end-times) concept held by some Christians, particularly those of American evangelicalism, consisting of an event when all dead Christian believers will be resurrected and, joined with Christians who are still alive, together will rise \"in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Teachings_of_Jesus_40_of_40._the_rapture._one_in_the_bed._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif/330px-Teachings_of_Jesus_40_of_40._the_rapture._one_in_the_bed._Jan_Luyken_etching._Bowyer_Bible.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rapture","wikidata":"Q870109"},{"title":"Rapture (iiO song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Rapture\" (sometimes referenced as \"Rapture (Tastes So Sweet)\") is a song by American recording duo iiO. It was chosen as the lead single from their debut studio album, Poetica (2005). The song was written by both the members, Nadia Ali and Markus Moser, while production was handled just by Moser. The song was released in the United Kingdom on October 29, 2001, by Made Records, Data Records, and Ministry of Sound. In the United States, it was released via Universal Records in January 2002."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6e/IiO_Rapture.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rapture_(iiO_song)","wikidata":"Q3071027"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thum